# Both GitHub Environments: staging and production. docs/GITHUB-ENVIRONMENTS.md
# Required SECRETS (7):
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# DATABASE_URL
# RESEND_API_KEY
# INTERNAL_DEPLOY_TOKEN
# RESTIC_PASSWORD
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# Required VARIABLES (9):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY
# MAIL_FROM
# MAIL_REPLY_TO
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION
# Optional VARIABLE:
# DATABASE_CA_CERT_BASE64
# NODE_IMAGE, REDIS_IMAGE, POSTGRES_IMAGE: only ops/image-pins.json, not Environment vars.
# AWS_* credentials come from Hetzner S3, not Amazon AWS.
# RESTIC_PASSWORD: create for new repository and keep in password vault.
# Turnstile private secret/OTP SMTP: Supabase Auth, not GitHub.
# Owner UUID/email/confirmation: temporary private operator config, never automatic deployment.
